    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Christian highland kingdom ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty">Solomonic dynasty</a>, which claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-of-sheba">Queen of Sheba</a>, from 1270 to 1974.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Adwa</a> in 1896 kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> independent and made it a symbol for pan-Africanists worldwide.</li><li>An unreformed feudal land system and the concealed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wollo-famine">Wollo famine</a> brought down <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> and the monarchy in 1974.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>'s survival in 1543 owed much to some 400 Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a>, whose firepower helped Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galawdewos">Galawdewos</a> defeat and kill <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad Gran</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wayna-daga">Wayna Daga</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

